  "body": "The README names the Tormach PathPilot post and the shipped Tormach mills, and no longer says setup sheets print alongside a post.\n\n### What changed (README only)\n\n- **Post:** adds Tormach PathPilot (`assets/posts/tormach.cps`, #131) to the list.\n- **Set up:** names the Tormach 770MX, 770MX (ML), 770M, 1100MX, 1500MX and PCNC 440 mills, which are in `posting::MACHINES` on `main`.\n- **Setup sheets:** replaces \"The setup sheet and tool list print alongside\" (Post never wrote them) with what exists. The Setups page lists each setup's tools in change order with cut and rapid lengths and estimated time, and **Export setup sheets...** writes one text page per setup. Posting does not write them.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/267-readme-posts.md`.\n\n### Not in this PR\n\n- The reporter couldn't find setup sheets because a new document can't reach the Setups page, or create a setup at all. The only controls that create one are on that page, and its browser row appears only once a setup exists. Triage notes on #267 and #45; the fix is #45's open part and moves the shell pixel snapshots (#255).\n- Making Post also write the sheet is the owner's call.\n\n### What ran\n\nDocs only, so no build or tests. I checked every name against `posting::BUILTINS` / `posting::MACHINES` and the Setups page code (`pages::tool_list_section`, `pages::sheet_footer`) on `main` 8f30bee.\n\nChangelog: The README names the Tormach PathPilot post and the shipped Tormach mills, and says setup sheets export from the Setups page (#267)\n\nRefs #267\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
